{"step_index":163,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T19:40:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-02T01:10:57+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-02T01:10:57+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/config/skills/youtube-channel-audit/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 334\nTotal Bytes: 12173\nShowing lines 1 to 334\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: youtube-channel-audit\n3: description: >\n4:   Automated YouTube channel audit and analysis using NexLev MCP tools.\n5:   Extracts channel profile, RPM, revenue, demographics, monetization status,\n6:   lifetime earnings, and per-video efficiency metrics. Outputs a structured\n7:   markdown report artifact. MUST activate whenever the user says \"analyze this\n8:   channel\", \"audit this channel\", \"channel analysis\", \"check this channel\",\n9:   \"how much is this channel earning\", \"do the same analysis\", \"do it for this\n10:   channel\", provides a YouTube channel screenshot, mentions a YouTube handle\n11:   (@username), or wants to know a channel's RPM, revenue, demographics, or\n12:   monetization status. Also activate when the user pastes a YouTube channel URL\n13:   or provides a channel name and wants financial/audience data. Activate even\n14:   when user says \"for this channel too\", \"same thing\", \"do it again\", or\n15:   provides just a screenshot of a YouTube channel page.\n16: ---\n17: \n18: # YouTube Channel Audit\n19: \n20: Run a complete NexLev-powered channel audit for any YouTube channel and output a structured markdown report artifact.\n21: \n22: ## When to Activate\n23: \n24: - User provides a channel handle (@username), screenshot, or URL\n25: - User says \"analyze\", \"audit\", \"check\", \"do the same\", \"for this channel too\"\n26: - User asks about RPM, revenue, earnings, demographics, monetization\n27: - User wants to compare channels\n28: - User sends a screenshot of a YouTube channel page\n29: \n30: ## Prerequisites\n31: \n32: - NexLev MCP caller skill must be installed at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\`\n33: - NexLev must be authenticated (tokens cached at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.mcp-auth\\`)\n34: - NEVER rewrite the NexLev caller scripts — just call them as-is\n35: \n36: ## Complete Audit Workflow\n37: \n38: Execute these steps in order for every channel analysis.\n39: \n40: ---\n41: \n42: ### Step 1: Extract Channel Handle\n43: \n44: Get the YouTube handle from the user's input:\n45: - **Screenshot**: Read the @handle visible in the channel page image\n46: - **URL**: Extract from `youtube.com/@handle`\n47: - **Text**: User says the handle or channel name directly\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ### Step 2: Fetch Channel Profile via NexLev\n52: \n53: Call `youtube_channel_about` with the handle:\n54: \n55: ```powershell\n56: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_audit.json\" -Value '{\"username\": \"HANDLE_HERE\"}' -Encoding UTF8\n57: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" youtube_channel_about \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_audit.json\"\n58: ```\n59: \n60: **Fields to extract from response:**\n61: \n62: | Field | JSON Key | Use |\n63: |-------|----------|-----|\n64: | Channel ID | `channelId` | Needed for ALL subsequent API calls |\n65: | Name | `title` | Report header |\n66: | Handle | `channelHandle` | Report header |\n67: | Subscribers | `subscriberCount` | Profile table |\n68: | Total Views | `viewCount` | Lifetime earnings calc |\n69: | Video Count | `videosCount` | Per-video efficiency calc |\n70: | Country | `country` | RPM context |\n71: | Join Date | `joinedDate` | Channel age calc |\n72: | Description | `description` | Content style identification |\n73: | Family Safe | `isFamilySafe` | COPPA risk indicator |\n74: | Has Email | `hasEmail` | Brand deal readiness |\n75: | Tabs | `tabs` | Check for \"Shorts\" tab |\n76: | Keywords | `keywords` | Niche identification |\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ### Step 3: Fetch RPM, Revenue & Demographics via NexLev\n81: \n82: Call `get_geography_revenue` with the channel ID from Step 2:\n83: \n84: ```powershell\n85: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_rpm.json\" -Value '{\"channelId\": \"CHANNEL_ID_HERE\"}' -Encoding UTF8\n86: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" get_geography_revenue \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_rpm.json\"\n87: ```\n88: \n89: **Fields to extract:**\n90: \n91: | Field | JSON Key | Use |\n92: |-------|----------|-----|\n93: | Monthly Revenue | `revenue.month_revenue` | Main revenue figure |\n94: | Long-form Revenue | `revenue.month_long_revenue` | Revenue breakdown |\n95: | Shorts Revenue | `revenue.month_short_revenue` | Revenue breakdown |\n96: | Long-form Views | `revenue.long_view_count` | Views breakdown |\n97: | Shorts Views | `revenue.short_view_count` | Views breakdown |\n98: | Category RPM | `revenue.channel_category_rpm` | Industry benchmark |\n99: | Channel Long RPM | `revenue.channel_long_rpm` | Actual earnings rate |\n100: | Channel Short RPM | `revenue.channel_short_rpm` | Shorts earnings rate |\n101: | Avg Duration | `revenue.weighted_avg_duration` | Content format |\n102: | Language | `revenue.channel_language_code` | Audience context |\n103: | Channel Type | `channelType` | LONG_ONLY / SHORT_ONLY / MIXED |\n104: | Category | `category` | Niche classification |\n105: | Gender | `demographics.gender` | Audience profile |\n106: | Age Groups | `demographics.age` | Audience profile |\n107: | Countries | `demographics.viewership_country` | Geographic distribution |\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ### Step 4: Monetization Check (Only if user explicitly requests)\n112: \n113: The user said \"don't give me monetisation check i will ultimately open their YouTube channel and watch the monetization check\" — so SKIP this by default. Only run if user explicitly asks.\n114: \n115: ```powershell\n116: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_mon.json\" -Value '{\"channelId\": \"CHANNEL_ID_HERE\"}' -Encoding UTF8\n117: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" check_channel_monetization \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_mon.json\"\n118: ```\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: ### Step 5: Calculate Derived Metrics\n123: \n124: From the raw data, compute these derived values:\n125: \n126: | Metric | Formula |\n127: |--------|---------|\n128: | **Lifetime Earnings** | `total_views × channel_long_rpm / 1000` |\n129: | **Channel Age (months)** | `(today - joinedDate) in months` |\n130: | **Average Monthly Earning** | `lifetime_earnings / channel_age_months` |\n131: | **Revenue per Video** | `lifetime_earnings / total_videos` |\n132: | **Views per Video** | `total_views / total_videos` |\n133: | **Subs per Video** | `subscribers / total_videos` |\n134: | **Tier 1 Traffic %** | `Sum of US + UK + Canada + Australia view percentages` |\n135: | **Growth Signal** | `current_monthly > avg_monthly = GROWING; else DECLINING` |\n136: \n137: ---\n138: \n139: ### Step 6: Generate Report Artifact\n140: \n141: Save the report as a markdown artifact: `{handle}_analysis.md`\n142: \n143: ## Report Template (Use This EXACT Structure)\n144: \n145: ```markdown\n146: # @{handle} ({channel_name}) — Full NexLev Channel Analysis\n147: \n148: > **All data sourced from NexLev MCP — zero assumptions.**\n149: > **Date**: {current_date}\n150: \n151: ---\n152: \n153: ## 1. Channel Profile (NexLev Data)\n154: \n155: | Field | Value |\n156: |-------|-------|\n157: | **Channel Name** | {name} |\n158: | **Handle** | @{handle} |\n159: | **Channel ID** | `{channelId}` |\n160: | **Country** | {country or \"Not set\"} |\n161: | **Joined** | {joinedDate} (**~{age_months} months ago**) |\n162: | **Subscribers** | {subscriberCount formatted with commas} |\n163: | **Total Views** | **{viewCount formatted}** |\n164: | **Videos** | {videosCount} |\n165: | **Has Shorts** | {Yes/No — check if \"Shorts\" in tabs array} |\n166: | **Avg Video Duration** | ~{weighted_avg_duration formatted as mm:ss} |\n167: | **Family Safe** | {isFamilySafe} |\n168: | **Has Contact Email** | {hasEmail} |\n169: | **Description** | \"{first 100 chars of description}\" |\n170: | **NexLev Category** | **{category}** |\n171: | **Content Style** | {1-line description inferred from keywords + description} |\n172: \n173: > Add a notable insight about the channel (e.g., uses TTS, no face, daily uploads).\n174: \n175: ---\n176: \n177: ## 2. RPM & Revenue (NexLev — Real Data)\n178: \n179: | Metric | Value |\n180: |--------|-------|\n181: | **Category RPM** | **${channel_category_rpm}** |\n182: | **Channel Long-form RPM** | **${channel_long_rpm}** |\n183: | **Channel Short RPM** | ${channel_short_rpm or \"N/A\"} |\n184: | **Estimated Monthly Revenue** | **${month_revenue formatted}** |\n185: | **Monthly Long-form Revenue** | ${month_long_revenue} |\n186: | **Monthly Shorts Revenue** | ${month_short_revenue or \"N/A\"} |\n187: | **Monthly Long-form Views** | {long_view_count formatted} |\n188: | **Monthly Shorts Views** | {short_view_count or \"N/A\"} |\n189: | **Channel Type** | {channelType} |\n190: | **Channel Language** | {channel_language_code} |\n191: \n192: ---\n193: \n194: ## 3. Total Lifetime Earnings Estimate\n195: \n196: | Calculation | Value |\n197: |------------|-------|\n198: | Total views | {viewCount} |\n199: | Channel RPM | ${channel_long_rpm} |\n200: | **Estimated total lifetime earnings** | **~${lifetime_earnings}** |\n201: | Months active | ~{channel_age_months} |\n202: | **Average monthly earning** | **~${avg_monthly}/month** |\n203: | **Current monthly earning** | **${month_revenue}/month** |\n204: | **Revenue per video** | **${rev_per_video}** |\n205: | **Views per video** | **{views_per_video}** |\n206: \n207: > Add growth signal: \"Channel is GROWING\" if current > average, \"DECLINING\" if lower.\n208: \n209: ---\n210: \n211: ## 4. Audience Demographics (NexLev — Real Data)\n212: \n213: ### Gender Split\n214: | Gender | % |\n215: |--------|---|\n216: | Male | {male_pct}% |\n217: | Female | {female_pct}% |\n218: \n219: ### Age Distribution\n220: | Age Group | % |\n221: |-----------|---|\n222: | 13-17 | {pct}% |\n223: | 18-24 | {pct}% |\n224: | 25-34 | {pct}% |\n225: | 35-44 | {pct}% |\n226: | 45-54 | {pct}% |\n227: | 55-64 | {pct}% |\n228: | 65+ | {pct}% |\n229: \n230: ### Top 5 Countries by Views\n231: | Country | % of Views |\n232: |---------|-----------|\n233: | {country_1} | {pct}% |\n234: | {country_2} | {pct}% |\n235: | {country_3} | {pct}% |\n236: | {country_4} | {pct}% |\n237: | {country_5} | {pct}% |\n238: \n239: > Add Tier 1 traffic insight and RPM impact.\n240: \n241: ---\n242: \n243: ## 5. Key Insight\n244: \n245: One paragraph highlighting the most important/surprising finding about this channel.\n246: \n247: ---\n248: \n249: ## 6. All Channels Comparison Table (if multiple channels analyzed in session)\n250: \n251: Include a comparison table with ALL previously analyzed channels if this isn't the first channel in the conversation.\n252: \n253: | Metric | Channel 1 | Channel 2 | ... | **This Channel** |\n254: |--------|-----------|-----------|-----|-------------------|\n255: | Niche | | | | |\n256: | Subs | | | | |\n257: | Views | | | | |\n258: | Videos | | | | |\n259: | Monthly Rev | | | | |\n260: | Lifetime | | | | |\n261: | Rev/Video | | | | |\n262: \n263: ---\n264: \n265: ## Data Sources\n266: \n267: | Data Point | NexLev Tool Used | Status |\n268: |-----------|-----------------|--------|\n269: | Channel profile | `youtube_channel_about` | ✅ |\n270: | RPM / Revenue / Demographics | `get_geography_revenue` | ✅ |\n271: | Monetization check | `check_channel_monetization` | ⬜ (not requested) |\n272: ```\n273: \n274: ---\n275: \n276: ## Rate Limit Awareness (NexLev FREE Plan)\n277: \n278: | Tool | Daily Limit | Priority |\n279: |------|-------------|----------|\n280: | `youtube_channel_about` | 50/day | Low concern |\n281: | `get_geography_revenue` | **5/day** | ⚠️ MOST LIMITED — plan carefully |\n282: | `check_channel_monetization` | 5/day | Only on request |\n283: | `youtube_channel_videos` | 50/day | Low concern |\n284: | `get_channel_analytics` | 5/day | Optional extras |\n285: | `get_niche_overview` | 5/day | For competitor research |\n286: \n287: If rate limited on `get_geography_revenue`, note it in the report and estimate revenue using similar channels from the same niche that were already analyzed.\n288: \n289: ## Error Handling\n290: \n291: | Error | Fix |\n292: |-------|-----|\n293: | Connection timeout / 502 | Retry once — NexLev servers occasionally drop |\n294: | \"Proactive token refresh failed\" | **IGNORE** — this is normal, not an error |\n295: | Auth/OAuth errors | Run `python nexlev_kill_stale.py` then retry |\n296: | Unicode errors on Windows | Prefix with `$env:PYTHONIOENCODING='utf-8'` |\n297: | Multi-line Python strings fail | Write Python code to a `.py` file first, then run it |\n298: \n299: ## Key Insights to Always Include\n300: \n301: After generating the raw data report, add contextual analysis covering:\n302: \n303: 1. **Growth trajectory**: Current monthly vs lifetime average — growing or declining?\n304: 2. **RPM vs category benchmark**: Above or below category average? Why?\n305: 3. **Shorts revenue trap**: If MIXED type, highlight how Shorts drag down effective RPM\n306: 4. **Geographic RPM impact**: High India/SEA traffic = lower RPM than category average\n307: 5. **Per-video efficiency**: Revenue per video compared to other analyzed channels\n308: 6. **Notable patterns**: TTS voice, faceless format, upload frequency, content formula\n309: 7. **Audience profile**: Who watches — gender skew, age concentration, parent vs direct viewer\n310: \n311: ## Batch Mode\n312: \n313: If the user wants multiple channels analyzed, use `nexlev_batch.py`:\n314: \n315: ```powershell\n316: # Create batch config\n317: Set-Content -Path \"batch.json\" -Value '[\n318:   {\"tool\": \"youtube_channel_about\", \"args\": {\"username\": \"handle1\"}},\n319:   {\"tool\": \"youtube_channel_about\", \"args\": {\"username\": \"handle2\"}}\n320: ]' -Encoding UTF8\n321: \n322: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_batch.py\" \"batch.json\"\n323: ```\n324: \n325: ## Channel ID Quick Reference\n326: \n327: When analyzing channels across a session, maintain a running table of channel IDs to avoid re-fetching:\n328: \n329: ```\n330: | Channel | Handle | ID |\n331: |---------|--------|----|\n332: | {name}  | @{handle} | {channelId} |\n333: ```\n334: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":164,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T19:40:58Z","content":"Here is the core methodology from the `youtube-channel-audit` skill, converted into a powerful, copy-pasteable prompt for the **vidIQ AI Coach**. \n\nSince we know NexLev's geo/RPM data is flawed for Hindi/unauthenticated channels, this prompt is designed to extract the *real* data vidIQ is good at (views, VPH, growth, competitors) and asks it to calculate realistic revenue based on language and niche.\n\n### Copy and Paste this into the vidIQ AI Coach:\n\n***\n\n**PROMPT FOR VIDIQ AI COACH:**\n\n```text\nAct as an expert YouTube Channel Auditor. I want you to run a deep-dive analysis on the following channel: \n[INSERT CHANNEL HANDLE/URL HERE]\n\nPlease structure your response into the following 5 sections:\n\n### 1. Channel Health & Velocity\n- What is the channel's 30-day view growth and subscriber growth?\n- What is their upload frequency (how many videos per week/month)?\n- Is this channel currently growing rapidly, stagnating, or declining?\n\n### 2. The \"Breakout\" Formula (VPH Analysis)\n- Identify their top 3 best-performing recent videos based on VPH (Views Per Hour).\n- What is the specific title format, topic, or thumbnail strategy they used in these breakout videos that made them succeed?\n- What is the estimated average duration of their videos?\n\n### 3. Competitor Landscape\n- List 3-5 similar channels in this specific micro-niche. \n- Are they the market leader, or is there a bigger channel dominating this space?\n\n### 4. Realistic Revenue Estimate (Language & Niche Adjusted)\nCalculate their estimated monthly revenue based on their 30-day views. *Do not use a generic global RPM.* Use the following realistic RPM logic based on the channel's language and niche:\n- If English (Finance/Business): Use $8.00 RPM\n- If English (Tech/Education/History): Use $4.00 RPM\n- If English (Gaming/Entertainment): Use $1.50 RPM\n- If Hindi (Education/Tech): Use $0.60 RPM\n- If Hindi (Entertainment/News/Gossip/Gaming): Use $0.30 RPM\nBased on this channel's language and content, what is their realistic monthly AdSense revenue?\n\n### 5. Replicability Score\nOn a scale of 1-10 (1 = extremely hard, 10 = very easy), how easy would it be for a solo creator to replicate this channel's content style? Consider factors like custom animation, on-camera presence, script research depth, and editing complexity.\n```\n\n***\n\n### Why this vidIQ prompt is better than the NexLev script:\n1. **It ignores fake demographics:** It skips asking for age/gender/country because we proved AI tools hallucinate that data for unauthenticated channels.\n2. **It forces realistic RPMs:** It feeds the AI the exact cheat-sheet we created ($0.30 for Hindi gossip, $4.00 for English tech, etc.) so the revenue estimate will actually be accurate.\n3. **It focuses on VPH (Views Per Hour):** This is vidIQ's superpower. Finding which videos are currently going viral is much more useful than knowing a channel's lifetime views from 8 years ago."}
